I have an idea for a new monster, called a walking wall.

These would be visually identical to ordinary walls and mindless (thus
impervious to telepathy), and bumping into them with a normal movement
command would give you the same message as a regular wall, but walking
walls would be distinguishable via monster detection, by watching to
see if they ever move (they would only get one move roughly every
dozen turns or so), by applying certain tools (e.g., drum of
earthquake would reveal their presence), by throwing things at them,
by deliberately attacking them (fight command), trying to dig through
them, trying to phase through them, or zapping certain wands or spells
at them.  In some cases, it would also be possible to just know that
there shouldn't be a wall in that location, although being late-game
monsters they would tend to occur in the mazes of Gehennom where this
is not so trivial.

Trying to dig through them, phase through them, or fight them in melee
would incur a passive attack.

Thrown weapons would not damage them.  As with any monster, the thrown
item would stop on the square where the monster is (rather than before
it, as with a normal wall), and you'd also get messages ("The first
elvish dagger misses.  The second elvish dagger hits it."  Walking
walls would normally be described as "it".)  Most melee weapons would
not hurt them very much, but pick-axes and mattocks would do rather
better.  (This could be implemented by just giving them a ton of hit
points and then making the picks do quadruple damage against them.)
Also, most melee weapons would have a chance of being dulled when
hitting them, but picks would not.

They would have no offensive attack, but they would defend themselves
if attacked.  There are several logical possibilities for the passive
attack, but I'm toying with the idea of stoning.  Obviously, they'd
have to be a relatively rare late-game monster if they do that.  If
that's too weird, ordinary physical damage is obvious, but it would
need to be fairly substantial.  (A late-game monster with an ordinary-
damage passive attack is just not threatening if it only does small-to-
moderate damage.)

Most pets would never attack them, but pets that tunnel or phase
through walls could run into them.

Most ray-type wands and spells would bounce off of them the same as
regular walls, making them effectively immune to sleep, lightning,
fire, cold, death rays, etc.  Wands and spells of teleport and
polymorph would handle them the same as any other monster.  Speed
monster would work normally but without giving any message (and
similarly slow monster, though they'd be so slow already that it
hardly seems relevant).  Digging and striking would injure them ("The
wall seems weaker now" or somesuch) but not necessarily kill them
outright.  Probing, knock/opening, secret door detection, and wands of
make invisible would give messages that a spoiled player could
interpret as meaning there's a walking wall there.  Cancellation would
eliminate their passive attack but without any message to clue the
player in to what has happened.

They would occur in small groups but would not be particularly common.

Thoughts?


